  {
   "role": "user",
   "kind": "normal",
   "timestamp": 1790344075460,
   "content": "Running the test suite leaves temporary directories behind in /tmp: right now there are about 3,200 directories named fuller-* (fuller-loop-*, fuller-home-*, fuller-outside-*, fuller-evaltasks-*, fuller-diff-home-*, fuller-diff-auto-*, fuller-mem-ws-*, fuller-mem-home-*, and others), and yesterday there were about 14,700 of them (1.1 GB). Each `npm test` run adds more.\n\nTask: make the test suite clean up after itself.\n1. Measure first: count the /tmp/fuller-* and /tmp/parity-* directories, run `npm test` once, count again, and report how many each run adds and with which prefixes (`ls -d /tmp/fuller-* | sed 's/-[^-]*$//' | sort | uniq -c` helps).\n2. Find every test file (tests/*.ts, tests/*.tsx) and helper that creates such directories (mkdtempSync / mkdtemp with these prefixes, also process.env.HOME set to a temp dir) without removing them: no afterEach/afterAll/try-finally with rmSync.\n3. Fix them with the smallest change that keeps the tests' behaviour: remove the directory in afterEach or afterAll (fs.rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true })), or a small shared helper if many files do the same thing. Do not touch the directories that already exist in /tmp (they belong to the user), and do not change production code in src/ for this.\n4. Verify: `npm run typecheck`, then `npm test` twice, counting the /tmp/fuller-* and /tmp/parity-* directories before and after each run. The count must not grow (a few directories created by processes that are killed mid-test are acceptable if you explain which ones). Report the before/after counts, the files you changed and why.",
   "tools": []
  },
